<article class="env-lemma" id="07BP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07BP">Lemma <span data-tag="07BP">10.134.6</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a surjective ring map with kernel $I$. Then $\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{B/A}$ is homotopy equivalent to the chain complex $(I/I^2 \to 0)$ with $I/I^2$ in degree $1$. In particular $H_1(L_{B/A}) = I/I^2$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/00S1" data-tag="00S1">10.134.2</a> and the fact that $A \to B$ is a presentation of $B$ over $A$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>